4. [DEFINITION] Finset set-builder notation elaborator
Module: Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic
Name: Mathlib.Meta.elabFinsetBuilderSetOf
Description: The elaborator for set-builder notation in finsets, which translates various forms of set comprehension into appropriate `Finset.filter` operations. Specifically, it handles the following cases:
1. `{x | p x}` becomes `Finset.filter (fun x ↦ p x) Finset.univ`
2. `{x : α | p x}` becomes `Finset.filter (fun x : α ↦ p x) Finset.univ`
3. `{x ∉ s | p x}` becomes `Finset.filter (fun x ↦ p x) sᶜ`
4. `{x ≠ a | p x}` becomes `Finset.filter (fun x ↦ p x) {a}ᶜ`

The elaborator checks that the expected type is a finset (not a set) before performing these translations.
Signature:  : TermElab

