Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.sum_const_nat
Description: For any finite set $s$ of type $\alpha$, a natural number $m$, and a function $f : \alpha \to \mathbb{N}$ such that $f(x) = m$ for all $x \in s$, the sum of $f$ over $s$ equals the cardinality of $s$ multiplied by $m$, i.e.,
$$\sum_{x \in s} f(x) = |s| \cdot m.$$
Signature:  {m : ℕ} {f : α → ℕ} (h₁ : ∀ x ∈ s, f x = m) : ∑ x ∈ s, f x = #s * m

5. [THEOREM] Expectation over Singleton Set Equals Function Value
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Expect
Name: Finset.expect_singleton
Description: For any function $f \colon \iota \to M$ where $M$ is an additively commutative monoid with scalar multiplication by nonnegative rational numbers, and for any element $i \in \iota$, the expectation (average) of $f$ over the singleton set $\{i\}$ is equal to $f(i)$, i.e.,
\[
\mathbb{E}_{j \in \{i\}} f(j) = f(i).
\]
Signature:  (f : ι → M) (i : ι) : 𝔼 j ∈ { i }, f j = f i

