1. [THEOREM] Multiplicative Property of Divisors: $\text{divisors}(m \cdot n) = \text{divisors}(m) \cdot \text{divisors}(n)$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.NatDivisors
Name: Nat.divisors_mul
Description: For any natural numbers $m$ and $n$, the set of divisors of their product $m \cdot n$ is equal to the product of the sets of divisors of $m$ and $n$ respectively. That is,
$$\text{divisors}(m \cdot n) = \text{divisors}(m) \cdot \text{divisors}(n).$$
Signature:  (m n : ℕ) : divisors (m * n) = divisors m * divisors n

2. [THEOREM] Upper Bound on Number of Divisors: $|\text{divisors}(n)| \leq n$
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.card_divisors_le_self
Description: For any natural number $n$, the number of divisors of $n$ is less than or equal to $n$ itself. In other words, $|\text{divisors}(n)| \leq n$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : #n.divisors ≤ n

3. [THEOREM] Maximum Divisor Equals the Number Itself
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.sup_divisors_id
Description: For any natural number $n$, the supremum (maximum) of the set of divisors of $n$ is equal to $n$ itself. In other words, $\max(\text{divisors}(n)) = n$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : n.divisors.sup id = n

4. [THEOREM] Self-Dual Property of Divisors under Division: $\{n/x \mid x \in \text{divisors}(n)\} = \text{divisors}(n)$
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.image_div_divisors_eq_divisors
Description: For any natural number $n$, the image of the function $x \mapsto n/x$ applied to the set of divisors of $n$ is equal to the set of divisors of $n$ itself. In symbols:
$$\left\{ \frac{n}{x} \mid x \in \text{divisors}(n) \right\} = \text{divisors}(n).$$
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : image (fun x : ℕ => n / x) n.divisors = n.divisors

5. [THEOREM] Sum of Divisors Equals Sum of Proper Divisors Plus Self
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.sum_divisors_eq_sum_properDivisors_add_self
Description: For any natural number $n$, the sum of all divisors of $n$ is equal to the sum of the proper divisors of $n$ plus $n$ itself, i.e.,
\[ \sum_{d \mid n} d = \left( \sum_{\substack{d \mid n \\ d \neq n}} d \right) + n. \]
Signature:  : ∑ i ∈ divisors n, i = (∑ i ∈ properDivisors n, i) + n

6. [THEOREM] Membership Characterization in Filtered Finite Set: $a \in s \text{ filter } p \leftrightarrow (a \in s \land p(a))$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.Filter
Name: Finset.mem_filter
Description: For any finite set $s$ of type $\alpha$ and any element $a \in \alpha$, the element $a$ belongs to the filtered set $s \text{ filter } p$ if and only if $a$ belongs to $s$ and satisfies the predicate $p$. In symbols:
$$a \in s \text{ filter } p \leftrightarrow a \in s \land p(a).$$
Signature:  {s : Finset α} {a : α} : a ∈ s.filter p ↔ a ∈ s ∧ p a
