2. [THEOREM] One is Not Prime
Module: Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs
Name: Nat.not_prime_one
Description: The natural number $1$ is not prime.
Signature:  : ¬Prime 1

3. [THEOREM] Sum of Indicators Equals Cardinality of Filtered Set
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring
Name: Finset.sum_boole
Description: For any decidable predicate $p$ on a type $\iota$ and any finite set $s$ of elements of $\iota$, the sum over $x \in s$ of $1$ if $p(x)$ holds and $0$ otherwise equals the cardinality of the filtered subset $\{x \in s \mid p(x)\}$ (interpreted as an element of an additive commutative monoid with one $\alpha$).
Signature:  (p) [DecidablePred p] (s : Finset ι) : (∑ x ∈ s, if p x then 1 else 0 : α) = #({x ∈ s | p x})

4. [THEOREM] Sum of Proper Divisors Divides Implies Sum is 1 or n
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.sum_properDivisors_dvd
Description: For a natural number $n$, if the sum of its proper divisors divides $n$, then this sum is either equal to $1$ or equal to $n$. In other words, if $\sum_{d \in \text{properDivisors}(n)} d$ divides $n$, then $\sum_{d \in \text{properDivisors}(n)} d = 1$ or $\sum_{d \in \text{properDivisors}(n)} d = n$.
Signature:  (h : (∑ x ∈ n.properDivisors, x) ∣ n) : ∑ x ∈ n.properDivisors, x = 1 ∨ ∑ x ∈ n.properDivisors, x = n

5. [THEOREM] Upper Bound on Number of Divisors: $|\text{divisors}(n)| \leq n$
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.card_divisors_le_self
Description: For any natural number $n$, the number of divisors of $n$ is less than or equal to $n$ itself. In other words, $|\text{divisors}(n)| \leq n$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : #n.divisors ≤ n

6. [THEOREM] Maximum Divisor Equals the Number Itself
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.sup_divisors_id
Description: For any natural number $n$, the supremum (maximum) of the set of divisors of $n$ is equal to $n$ itself. In other words, $\max(\text{divisors}(n)) = n$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : n.divisors.sup id = n

7. [THEOREM] Non-primality of Zero
Module: Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs
Name: Nat.not_prime_zero
Description: The natural number $0$ is not prime.
Signature:  : ¬Prime 0

8. [THEOREM] Self-Dual Property of Divisors under Division: $\{n/x \mid x \in \text{divisors}(n)\} = \text{divisors}(n)$
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.image_div_divisors_eq_divisors
Description: For any natural number $n$, the image of the function $x \mapsto n/x$ applied to the set of divisors of $n$ is equal to the set of divisors of $n$ itself. In symbols:
$$\left\{ \frac{n}{x} \mid x \in \text{divisors}(n) \right\} = \text{divisors}(n).$$
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : image (fun x : ℕ => n / x) n.divisors = n.divisors

9. [THEOREM] Sum of Divisors Formula via Prime Factorization: $\sum_{d \mid n} d = \prod_{p \mid n} \sum_{k=0}^{v_p(n)} p^k$
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction
Name: Nat.sum_divisors
Description: For any nonzero natural number $n$, the sum of its divisors equals the product over its prime factors $p$ of the sum of powers $p^k$ for $k$ from $0$ to the exponent of $p$ in the factorization of $n$. That is,
\[
\sum_{d \mid n} d = \prod_{p \mid n} \sum_{k=0}^{v_p(n)} p^k,
\]
where $v_p(n)$ denotes the exponent of the prime $p$ in the factorization of $n$.
Signature:  {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0) : ∑ d ∈ n.divisors, d = ∏ p ∈ n.primeFactors, ∑ k ∈ .range (n.factorization p + 1), p ^ k

10. [THEOREM] Product of Non-One Natural Numbers is Not Prime
Module: Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic
Name: Nat.not_prime_mul
Description: For any natural numbers $a$ and $b$ such that $a \neq 1$ and $b \neq 1$, the product $a \times b$ is not a prime number.
Signature:  {a b : ℕ} (a1 : a ≠ 1) (b1 : b ≠ 1) : ¬Prime (a * b)

11. [THEOREM] Empty Proper Divisors Condition: $\text{properDivisors}(n) = \emptyset \leftrightarrow n \leq 1$
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.properDivisors_eq_empty
Description: For any natural number $n$, the set of proper divisors of $n$ is empty if and only if $n \leq 1$.
Signature:  : n.properDivisors = ∅ ↔ n ≤ 1

12. [THEOREM] Sum of Divisors Equals Sum of Proper Divisors Plus Self
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.sum_divisors_eq_sum_properDivisors_add_self
Description: For any natural number $n$, the sum of all divisors of $n$ is equal to the sum of the proper divisors of $n$ plus $n$ itself, i.e.,
\[ \sum_{d \mid n} d = \left( \sum_{\substack{d \mid n \\ d \neq n}} d \right) + n. \]
Signature:  : ∑ i ∈ divisors n, i = (∑ i ∈ properDivisors n, i) + n

13. [THEOREM] Sum of Divisors Multiplicative Property for Coprime Numbers
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction
Name: Nat.Coprime.sum_divisors_mul
Description: For any two coprime natural numbers $m$ and $n$, the sum of the divisors of their product $m \cdot n$ equals the product of the sums of the divisors of $m$ and $n$ respectively. That is,
\[ \sum_{d \mid (m \cdot n)} d = \left( \sum_{d \mid m} d \right) \cdot \left( \sum_{d \mid n} d \right). \]
Signature:  {m n : ℕ} (hmn : m.Coprime n) : ∑ d ∈ (m * n).divisors, d = (∑ d ∈ m.divisors, d) * ∑ d ∈ n.divisors, d

14. [THEOREM] Sum of Proper Divisors Equals One if and only if Prime
Module: Mathlib.NumberTheory.Divisors
Name: Nat.sum_properDivisors_eq_one_iff_prime
Description: For a natural number $n$, the sum of its proper divisors equals $1$ if and only if $n$ is a prime number. In other words, $\sum_{x \in \text{properDivisors}(n)} x = 1 \leftrightarrow \text{Prime}(n)$.
Signature:  : ∑ x ∈ n.properDivisors, x = 1 ↔ n.Prime
