1. [THEOREM] Filtered Set Equals Original Set if and only if All Elements Satisfy Predicate
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.Filter
Name: Finset.filter_eq_self
Description: For a finite set $s$ and a decidable predicate $p$, the filtered set $s \text{ filter } p$ equals $s$ if and only if every element $x$ in $s$ satisfies $p(x)$. In other words:
$$ \{x \in s \mid p(x)\} = s \iff \forall x \in s, p(x) $$
