2. [THEOREM] Membership Characterization in Filtered Finite Set: $a \in s \text{ filter } p \leftrightarrow (a \in s \land p(a))$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.Filter
Name: Finset.mem_filter
Description: For any finite set $s$ of type $\alpha$ and any element $a \in \alpha$, the element $a$ belongs to the filtered set $s \text{ filter } p$ if and only if $a$ belongs to $s$ and satisfies the predicate $p$. In symbols:
$$a \in s \text{ filter } p \leftrightarrow a \in s \land p(a).$$
Signature:  {s : Finset α} {a : α} : a ∈ s.filter p ↔ a ∈ s ∧ p a

3. [THEOREM] Filtering with Constant Predicate: $\{x \in s \mid p\} = \text{if } p \text{ then } s \text{ else } \emptyset$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.Filter
Name: Finset.filter_const
Description: For any finite set $s$ of type $\alpha$ and any proposition $p$ (with a decidability instance), the filtered set $\{x \in s \mid p\}$ equals $s$ if $p$ is true, and equals the empty set $\emptyset$ if $p$ is false.
Signature:  (p : Prop) [Decidable p] (s : Finset α) : (s.filter fun _a => p) = if p then s else ∅

4. [DEFINITION] Filtering elements in a finite set by a predicate
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.Filter
Name: Finset.filter
Description: Given a decidable predicate \( p : \alpha \to \text{Prop} \) and a finite set \( s \) of type \( \alpha \), the operation \( \text{filter } p \ s \) returns the finite subset of \( s \) consisting of all elements that satisfy \( p \). For example, \( s \text{ filter } (\cdot \in t) \) gives the intersection of \( s \) with another set \( t \) when the membership is decidable.
Signature:  (s : Finset α) : Finset α

5. [THEOREM] Composition of Finite Set Filters via Conjunction
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finset.Filter
Name: Finset.filter_filter
Description: For any finite set $s$ of type $\alpha$ and predicates $p, q : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$, the result of first filtering $s$ by $p$ and then filtering the result by $q$ is equal to filtering $s$ by the conjunction $p(a) \land q(a)$ for each element $a \in s$. In other words, $(s \text{ filter } p) \text{ filter } q = s \text{ filter } (\lambda a, p(a) \land q(a))$.
Signature:  (s : Finset α) : (s.filter p).filter q = s.filter fun a => p a ∧ q a

