1. [THEOREM] Reminder equality under congruence and bound condition
Module: Mathlib.Data.Nat.ModEq
Name: Nat.mod_eq_of_modEq
Description: For natural numbers $a$, $b$, and $n$, if $a \equiv b \pmod{n}$ and $b < n$, then the remainder of $a$ divided by $n$ is equal to $b$, i.e., $a \% n = b$.
Signature:  {a b n} (h : a ≡ b [MOD n]) (hb : b < n) : a % n = b

2. [THEOREM] Equality in $\mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}$ via Natural Number Congruence
Module: Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
Name: ZMod.natCast_eq_natCast_iff
Description: For any natural numbers $a$, $b$, and $c$, the images of $a$ and $b$ in $\mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}$ are equal if and only if $a$ is congruent to $b$ modulo $c$, i.e., $(a : \mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}) = (b : \mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}) \leftrightarrow a \equiv b \pmod{c}$.
Signature:  (a b c : ℕ) : (a : ZMod c) = (b : ZMod c) ↔ a ≡ b [MOD c]

3. [THEOREM] Equality in $\mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}$ via Remainder Equality
Module: Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
Name: ZMod.natCast_eq_natCast_iff'
Description: For any natural numbers $a$, $b$, and $c$, the images of $a$ and $b$ in $\mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}$ are equal if and only if the remainders of $a$ and $b$ modulo $c$ are equal, i.e., $(a : \mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}) = (b : \mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}) \leftrightarrow a \bmod c = b \bmod c$.
Signature:  (a b c : ℕ) : (a : ZMod c) = (b : ZMod c) ↔ a % c = b % c
