2. [THEOREM] Modulo of Sum as Conditional Expression
Module: Mathlib.Data.Nat.Defs
Name: Nat.add_mod_eq_ite
Description: For any natural numbers $m$, $n$, and $k$, the modulo of the sum $m + n$ with respect to $k$ equals:
- $(m \bmod k + n \bmod k) - k$ if $k \leq (m \bmod k + n \bmod k)$,
- $m \bmod k + n \bmod k$ otherwise.
Signature:  : (m + n) % k = if k ≤ m % k + n % k then m % k + n % k - k else m % k + n % k

3. [THEOREM] Modulo Equals Dividend if and only if Dividend is Less Than Divisor
Module: Mathlib.Data.Nat.Defs
Name: Nat.mod_eq_iff_lt
Description: For any natural numbers $m$ and $n$ with $n \neq 0$, the remainder of $m$ divided by $n$ equals $m$ if and only if $m$ is strictly less than $n$. In other words:
$$m \bmod n = m \leftrightarrow m < n$$
Signature:  (hn : n ≠ 0) : m % n = m ↔ m < n

