1. [THEOREM] Negation Equals Self in $\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}$ iff Zero or Twice Representative Equals Modulus
Module: Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
Name: ZMod.neg_eq_self_iff
Description: For any natural number $n$ and any element $a \in \mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}$, the negation of $a$ equals $a$ itself if and only if either $a$ is zero or twice the canonical representative value of $a$ equals $n$. That is, $-a = a \leftrightarrow (a = 0 \lor 2 \cdot \mathrm{val}(a) = n)$.
Signature:  {n : ℕ} (a : ZMod n) : -a = a ↔ a = 0 ∨ 2 * a.val = n

2. [THEOREM] Left Cancellation Property of Integer Congruence: $c + a \equiv c + b \pmod{n} \Rightarrow a \equiv b \pmod{n}$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Int.ModEq
Name: Int.ModEq.add_left_cancel'
Description: For any integers $a$, $b$, $c$, and $n$, if $c + a \equiv c + b \pmod{n}$, then $a \equiv b \pmod{n}$.
Signature:  (c : ℤ) (h : c + a ≡ c + b [ZMOD n]) : a ≡ b [ZMOD n]

3. [THEOREM] Equality in $\mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}$ via Natural Number Congruence
Module: Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
Name: ZMod.natCast_eq_natCast_iff
Description: For any natural numbers $a$, $b$, and $c$, the images of $a$ and $b$ in $\mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}$ are equal if and only if $a$ is congruent to $b$ modulo $c$, i.e., $(a : \mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}) = (b : \mathbb{Z}/c\mathbb{Z}) \leftrightarrow a \equiv b \pmod{c}$.
Signature:  (a b c : ℕ) : (a : ZMod c) = (b : ZMod c) ↔ a ≡ b [MOD c]

4. [THEOREM] Natural Number Image Zero in $\mathbb{Z}/b\mathbb{Z}$ iff $b$ Divides $a$
Module: Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
Name: ZMod.natCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd
Description: For any natural numbers $a$ and $b$, the image of $a$ in $\mathbb{Z}/b\mathbb{Z}$ is zero if and only if $b$ divides $a$, i.e., $(a : \mathbb{Z}/b\mathbb{Z}) = 0 \leftrightarrow b \mid a$.
Signature:  (a b : ℕ) : (a : ZMod b) = 0 ↔ b ∣ a

5. [THEOREM] $n \equiv 0$ in $\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}$
Module: Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic
Name: ZMod.natCast_self
Description: For any natural number $n$, the canonical image of $n$ in the ring of integers modulo $n$ is zero, i.e., $n \equiv 0 \pmod{n}$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : (n : ZMod n) = 0
